<title>LATVIA: Latvia says oil transit rose 14 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Latvia says oil transit rose 14 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic state of Latvia, one of the main outlets for Russian crude oil, said on Friday that some 20.7 million tonnes of oil and oil products were transported through it in 1996, 14 percent more than in 1995.</p>
<p>The statistics office said in a statement that transit of crude oil rose from 15.2 million tonnes (some 304,000 barrels per day) in 1995 to 18 million tonnes (360,000 bpd) in 1996. The transit of oil products dipped by 180,000 tonnes to 2.7 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Most of the oil transported through Latvia from Russia goes through the oil terminal of Ventspils in western Latvia.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Riga Newsroom +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
